[block
  'ORD-0002-icons'
  [ctx
    'the spec of EMS-003'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-003/EMS-003.pgml'
  [/ctx]
  [ctx
    'the signed model'
    '.guidelines/.orders/INTAKE-2D-VIEW.md, section 6'
  [/ctx]
  [ctx
    'the icons as delivered'
    '.scope/asset/glyph-icons'
  [/ctx]
  [tgt
    'the icons enter the app as one set a table names: every command of the vocabulary answers an icon or a declared fallback, drawn in the colours of the interface'
  [/tgt]
  [ctx
    'measured at c078f2c: the 41 files hold the fills black and white written in, and two of them a third colour; four tile sizes, 13 by 17, 13 by 18, 14 by 17 and 15 by 18, and 8 by 8 for the two pins; each tile carries its name drawn as outlines above it, and nt.svg carries the word note'
  [/ctx]
  [ctx
    'measured at c078f2c: by category the set covers action 4 of 10, judgement 9 of 16, question 2 of 4, framing 1 of 8, context 3 of 5, condition 5 of 9, limit 4 of 12, reasoning 0 of 14, course 2 of 6, intensity 1 of 4, frame 3 of 10 and mark 2 of 6'
  [/ctx]
  [ins
    'normalise the set into the app: one tile size, the colours taken from the interface and never written in the file, and the name drawn by the page from the vocabulary'
  [/ins]
  [ins
    'write the icon table from the files, never by hand: each command, its icon or its fallback, and the icons no command names'
  [/ins]
  [req
    'a command with no icon shows a fallback tile with its name, and the table says which commands those are'
  [/req]
  [cnst
    'the delivered files stay as delivered in .scope; the normalised set is generated from them by a script, and a generated file is never edited by hand'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'the interface is a black background with cyan, purple, dark green and light blue, and nothing greyish'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'no icon is drawn that the Regent did not deliver: the 81 commands with none are listed for the Regent, and the fallback answers until an icon arrives'
  [/cnst]
  [cmp
    'the table'
    'npm run check refuses an icon no command names and no exception declares, a command the table leaves out, and a normalised file that differs from a fresh build, each seen failing before it counts'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
  [sub
    [eq
      [cmp
        [ctx[/ctx]
      [/cmp]
    [/eq]
  [/sub]
  [elab
    [eq[/eq]
    [sub[/sub]
    [rsn[/rsn]
  [/elab]
  [ref
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/ref]
  [ctx[/ctx]
  [core[/core]
  [core[/core]
  [elab[/elab]
  [cmp
    'the set'
    'every tile renders at one size in the colours of the interface, measured on the page in the browser of the repository'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
  [sub
    [eq
      [cmp
        [ctx[/ctx]
      [/cmp]
    [/eq]
  [/sub]
